# Canonical identities for `git log`, `git shortlog` and `git blame`.
#
# This file only changes how names DISPLAY. It rewrites no commits, moves no
# history, and GitHub's contributor graph ignores it entirely — that graph keys
# off the author email, so merging the two accounts there means adding
# FlimtotheFlam@gmail.com to the DimitroffVodka GitHub account, not editing
# anything here.
#
# Format: <canonical name> <canonical email> [<old name>] <old email>

# ── One person, four git identities ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 709 commits went in as FlimtotheFlam, 226 + 78 as two spellings of
# Dimitroffvodka, and 25 more as FlimtotheFlam wearing the other email. Same
# author throughout; only the git config differed at the time.
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> <FlimtotheFlam@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> <DimitroffVodka@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> FlimtotheFlam <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> Dimitroffvodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com>

# ── Assistants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELIBERATELY NOT folded into the human above. 33 commits have Claude as the
# git author rather than as a co-author trailer, and those were genuinely
# written by it — displaying them as a person's work would be a false claim
# about who wrote the code, which is the opposite of what a mailmap is for.
#
# What this does collapse is the fifteen model-name variants that accumulated
# in Co-Authored-By trailers (Opus 4.6/4.7/4.8/5, Fable 5, Sonnet 4.6, the 1M
# context suffixes) into one entry, so `git shortlog --group=trailer:co-authored-by`
# reports Claude once instead of fifteen times.
Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>

# The other assistants keep their own identities — separate vendors, separate
# emails, and nothing to normalise.
